From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 19:50:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] netifd: set up again a device that the kernel deleted

netifd took the kernel's removal of a device into account only for the
devices it did not create. When the kernel deleted one it had created,
as it deletes a vxlan with its lower device, netifd kept the device as
present and up, and neither a reload nor an ifup created it again. A
vxlan whose tunnel link is a bridge's vlan device was lost this way
when netifd set the vlan device up again on a change of the bridge's
ports (B35/B42: an Aeolus tunnel, until netifd restarted).

002 cycles such a device's presence, as a restarting configuration
change does, so its users claim it again and it is created anew. 003
lets a bridge retry a member that failed to come up when it was added,
for a vxlan created again before its lower device is back. Both are
upstream netifd commits on openwrt/netifd, sent as a pull request.

Bump PKG_RELEASE.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 package/network/config/netifd/Makefile        |  2 +-
 ...device-again-that-the-kernel-deleted.patch | 62 +++++++++++++++++++
 ...at-fails-to-come-up-when-it-is-added.patch | 45 ++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 108 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100755 package/network/config/netifd/patches/002-device-set-up-a-device-again-that-the-kernel-deleted.patch
 create mode 100755 package/network/config/netifd/patches/003-bridge-retry-a-member-that-fails-to-come-up-when-it-is-added.patch

diff --git a/package/network/config/netifd/Makefile b/package/network/config/netifd/Makefile
index 6eaba948bd..bf8c69d0bf 100644
--- a/package/network/config/netifd/Makefile
+++ b/package/network/config/netifd/Makefile
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=netifd
-PKG_RELEASE:=2
+PKG_RELEASE:=3
 
 PKG_SOURCE_PROTO:=git
 PKG_SOURCE_URL=$(PROJECT_GIT)/project/netifd.git
diff --git a/package/network/config/netifd/patches/002-device-set-up-a-device-again-that-the-kernel-deleted.patch b/package/network/config/netifd/patches/002-device-set-up-a-device-again-that-the-kernel-deleted.patch
